(a) Not later than ten years after the construction and establishment of the first New York state veterans cemetery, and every ten years thereafter, the department, in cooperation with the United States department of veterans affairs, shall conduct an investigation and study on the issue of the construction and establishment of additional New York state veterans cemeteries. Such investigation and study shall consider, but not be limited to, the study parameters established pursuant to paragraph (a) of subdivision two of this section. A report of the investigation and study required to be conducted pursuant to this subdivision shall be delivered to the governor, the temporary president of the senate, the speaker of the assembly and the chair of the senate committee on veterans, homeland security and military affairs, and the chair of the assembly committee on veterans' affairs, by no later than ninety days after the department has commenced the conduct of the investigation and study;

